#!/usr/bin/env python3
# chezmoi modify_ script for ~/.config/herdr-app/layouts/neon.json.
#
# The layout is BASE below; edit it here, not in the target file. Herdr itself
# rewrites the target: the background rotation (mods/tmux-bar/backgrounds.js)
# sets the root "background" through layout.set, which for a personal layout
# saves the whole tree back to the file (its own key order, f32 numbers, and
# folded-in clicks like the sidebar width). So:
#
# - the root background is runtime state: the current one is always kept;
# - when the file matches BASE apart from that, it is left untouched, so
#   chezmoi sees no difference;
# - otherwise BASE is written, with the current background.
